{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.PhiQJSJ","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.PhiQPiece","lean:module:QOU.Kashaev","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.bridge_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.bridge_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L101-L111","doc":"**Non-negativity of the bridge value.**\n\nBoth sides of the bridge equation are non-negative: the\narchimedean realisation is non-negative by hypothesis, and\nthe right-hand side is the product of `ρ q > 0` (when\n`1 < q`) and the non-negative piece volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.bridge","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L80-L99","doc":"**Master conditional bridge theorem.**\n\nFor every braid `β`, the archimedean realisation of the\nper-`S` dilog summand equals `ρ_q · Vol_hyp(K_S)`.  This is the\nstatement of `conj:phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge`, fully verified by\nLean **modulo** the typeclass instance `[PerPieceBridge q]`,\nwhich in turn depends on `[VolumeConjecture q]` (Kashaev) and\n`[TowerSummandRealization q]` (realisation infrastructure).\n\nNo `sorry`: every step is either definitional or supplied by a\ntypeclass field. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge","label":"rem:phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-tower-jsj-bridge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridge.bridge_per_piece","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridge.bridge_per_piece","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.PerPieceBridge","kind":"class","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L64-L78","doc":"**Φ_q–JSJ archimedean bridge (per-piece).**\n\nConditional on `Kashaev.VolumeConjecture q` and a\n`TowerSummandRealization q` instance, the archimedean realisation\nof the per-`S` dilog summand equals `ρ_q · Vol_hyp(K_S)`.\n\nThe class field `bridge_per_piece` plays the role of the\n`kvc_holds`-style axiom: it is the per-piece identification\nthat the conjecture asserts, lifted to a typeclass field so\ndownstream theorems can consume it abstractly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.TowerSummandRealization.realisation_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.TowerSummandRealization.realisation_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The realisation is non-negative (real volumes are non-negative). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.TowerSummandRealization.realisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.TowerSummandRealization.realisation","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Archimedean realisation of the per-`S` dilog summand of the\ntower (with the appropriate Markov weight `z^|S|` already\nabsorbed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.TowerSummandRealization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.TowerSummandRealization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.TowerSummandRealization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.TowerSummandRealization","kind":"class","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L47-L62","doc":"Archimedean realisation of the dilogarithm form of the per-`S`\nsummand of the tower.  This is the **target** of the bridge: it\nis the real number that `Φ_q(V_S)` (resp. `z² · Φ_q(V_i V_j)`)\nrealises to under `τ_arch = π_∞ ∘ τ`.\n\nAxiomatised here so the bridge theorem can be stated without\nimporting the full archimedean-realisation infrastructure;\npopulated by any concrete instance of the realisation functor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.rho_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.rho_pos","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L43-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.PhiQJSJ.rho","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.PhiQJSJ.rho","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/PhiQJSJ.lean#L40-L41","doc":"The substrate density `ρ_q = 1/ℏ_q²`, with `ℏ_q = (q-1)/q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}